[usage-help] exit=0
   jackin❯


Read cached usage and quota data from a running Capsule daemon

Usage: jackin usage [OPTIONS] [INSTANCE] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  accounts    Show cached provider account/quota buckets
  verify      Verify all provider quota rows are present and trusted
  doctor      Run passive readiness checks without accessing credentials or providers
  service     Manage the local usage broker
  monitor     Manage an unattended quota monitor
  binding     Confirm a local monitor-account to source-scope mapping for quota monitoring
  policy      Approve a durable quota-monitor policy for a bound account and goal
  status      Read the status of a durable monitor
  refresh     Reconcile a monitor against local evidence without provider refresh
  watch       Stream new monitor events as JSON Lines
  wait        Wait for runnable evidence for a bounded time
  statusline  Ingest or compose Claude Code statusline integration
  spend       Record an explicit account-bound spend baseline
  auth        Prepare provider authentication in an attached terminal

Arguments:
  [INSTANCE]
          Instance name for Capsule account inspection, or `cache` for the host account cache

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          [default: human]

      --data-dir <PATH>
          Use an isolated jackin data directory for this usage operation

      --debug
          Print raw container output for troubleshooting.

          Global flag: accepted before or after any subcommand. Also enabled by setting `JACKIN_DEBUG=1` in the environment.

          [env: JACKIN_DEBUG=]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
